  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA 4K AE2 (BRAVIA_AE2, MediaTek MT5897 \"merak\"), North American firmware\nGoogle TV 14 (API 34), build BRAVIA_AE2_NA-user 14 UKN4.250422.001 603100\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-bravia-ae2/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-bravia-ae2/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx (pass it as STOCK_LAUNCHER / to restore.sh).\nNo separate Live TV app on this set: HDMI inputs come from TvInputManager, so leave live_tv_package empty.\nKeep the com.sony.dtv.tvinput.* HDMI services, com.sony.dtv.tvapi, com.sony.dtv.sonysystemservice\nand the Sony settings apps: they drive HDMI, picture settings and the remote.\n\nQuirks on this firmware, all checked on the TV:\n- Network ADB: pair once with Wireless debugging (`adb pair <ip>:<port> <code>`, then\n`adb connect` to the port `adb mdns services` shows), then `adb tcpip 5555` for tools/tv.py.\nPort 5555 closes again after a reboot.\n- com.google.android.tungsten.setupwraith claims HOME with priority 1 (RecoveryActivity); disable it\nbefore launcherx or Home can land on it.\n- The default screensaver is com.sony.dtv.livingfit; with it disabled the TV has none until you\npick another (the launcher's Clock: `settings put secure screensaver_components\ncom.gathin.tvhome/.ClockDream`).\n- YouTube Music for TV (com.google.android.youtube.tvmusic) ends its media session when you leave it,\nso music stops on Home; SoundCloud keeps playing.\n\nMost of this list was disabled by the owner before the launcher went on and has been lived with;\nthe Sony agents, help and Play extras marked (new) were added on 19 October 2026. If something\nbreaks, re-enable it with `pm enable <package>` and please report it.\ntracking / ads / recommendations",
